WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.153
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:15.611
Unit nine: Solving Problems. In this unit, you will talk about problems and find solutions.

4
00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:17.444
Problem.

5
00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:20.747
Problem means something difficult that you need to fix.

6
00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:23.711
My bike has a problem. The tire is flat.

7
00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:26.750
Your turn. Say: Problem.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.265
Problem.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.123
Solution.

10
00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:35.322
Solution means a way to fix a problem.

11
00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:37.448
We found a solution together.

12
00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:40.800
Your turn. Say: Solution.

13
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.431
Solution.

14
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:46.302
Idea.

15
00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:49.280
Idea means a thought or a plan in your mind.

16
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.022
I have a great idea!

17
00:00:51.722 --> 00:00:54.212
Your turn. Say: Idea.

18
00:00:56.912 --> 00:00:57.623
Idea.

19
00:00:58.617 --> 00:00:59.420
Try.

20
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.329
Try means to make an effort to do something.

21
00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.770
Try again. You can do it!

22
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.100
Your turn. Say: Try.

23
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.545
Try.

24
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.156
Think.

25
00:01:13.856 --> 00:01:15.508
Think means to use your mind.

26
00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.343
Let me think for a minute.

27
00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:20.533
Your turn. Say: Think.

28
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:23.967
Think.

29
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:25.928
Mistake.

30
00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:28.685
Mistake means something that is wrong.

31
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:30.799
Everyone makes mistakes.

32
00:01:31.499 --> 00:01:34.430
Your turn. Say: Mistake.

33
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:37.980
Mistake.

34
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:39.799
Ask.

35
00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.555
Ask means to say a question to get help or information.

36
00:01:43.855 --> 00:01:46.342
If you don't understand, ask the teacher.

37
00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:49.834
Your turn. Say: Ask.

38
00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:53.349
Ask.

39
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.177
Again.

40
00:01:55.877 --> 00:01:57.563
Again means one more time.

41
00:01:57.863 --> 00:01:59.247
Read the question again.

42
00:01:59.947 --> 00:02:02.576
Your turn. Say: Again.

43
00:02:05.276 --> 00:02:06.092
Again.

44
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.187
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.487 --> 00:02:12.651
Sreypich, you look worried. What's the problem?

46
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.950
I can't solve this math question.

47
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.958
If you read it again, you see the key words.

48
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.843
Oh! If I draw a picture, I understand it better.

49
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.756
Good idea! And if you still don't know?

50
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.409
If I don't know, I ask for help.

51
00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:37.295
Grammar focus: If plus present, I plus verb.

52
00:02:37.595 --> 00:02:39.989
If I make a mistake, I try again.

53
00:02:40.289 --> 00:02:42.928
Put a comma after the 'if' part when it comes first.

54
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.453
Now read and listen. Never Give Up.

55
00:02:46.753 --> 00:02:48.857
Everyone has problems sometimes.

56
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.136
If I have a problem with homework, I think carefully first.

57
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.796
If I don't understand, I ask my teacher or a friend.

58
00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:03.524
If I make a mistake, I don't feel sad. I try again.

59
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.664
Every problem has a solution if we keep trying.

60
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.486
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.786 --> 00:03:14.239
If I don't understand, I blank the teacher.

62
00:03:14.539 --> 00:03:18.122
A, ask. B, asked. C, asking.

63
00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:24.081
The answer is A: ask.

64
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:27.560
A way to fix a problem is a blank.

65
00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.734
A, solution. B, mistake. C, problem.

66
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.552
The answer is A: solution.

67
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.713
One more time means blank.

68
00:03:41.013 --> 00:03:44.295
A, again. B, never. C, already.

69
00:03:48.283 --> 00:03:50.364
The answer is A: again.

70
00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.199
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you do if you have a problem?

71
00:04:00.499 --> 00:04:06.449
If I have a problem, I think carefully. If I can't solve it, I ask my teacher for help, and I try again.

72
00:04:06.749 --> 00:04:08.829
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:09.817 --> 00:04:14.942
Great work today! You learned eight new words and if plus present, i plus verb.

74
00:04:15.242 --> 00:04:19.496
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

75
00:04:19.796 --> 00:04:22.391
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

76
00:04:22.691 --> 00:04:25.111
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

